{
  "description": "A type as the pack writes it (OBJ frame) -> where each inner door's bridge meets the floor, as the floor check finds it (FloorCheck.bridgeSides): for each door in order, the pieces of the floor with every door between zones shut (FloorRegion by Interior.region(0.3, doors, 0), model frame, Z order: floor_region's pieces) that the door's bridge (FloorCheck.bridge: its span less 0.1 at each end, 0.6 past its faces) touches before its leaf (a piece ending at or short of the leaf's cut along the door's axis, -X or -Z of the model frame) and behind it, and on how many sides it reaches the floor: both, one or none (BridgeSides.Reach.key); null for a hull or gangway door. The rule of INNER_DOOR_NO_FLOOR (none) and INNER_DOOR_FLOOR_ROUND (both sides one floor), and of the editor's doors tool, which shows a bridge reaching the floor on one side only. input.bridges_of: the type; expected: the list, or null if the type has no floor.",
  "frame": "none",
  "tolerance": 0,
  "cases": [
    {
